            <ArticleTitle>Cryosurgery in the management of intractable facial pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>135-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The biological sequelae to the experimental freezing of peripheral nerves have been shown to differ in several respects from those following other types of nerve injury. A clinical application of these effects utilising the extreme low temperature produced by modern cryosurgical equipment is proposed and a preliminary evaluation is made.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
